# Signed artefacts are BYTES, not text. Git must never touch them.
#
# Without this, git's line-ending heuristics convert LF to CRLF on checkout for
# anyone on Windows — and a signed document whose bytes changed is a signed
# document that no longer verifies. The signature would still be present, still
# look right, and fail for every reader who cloned the repository. Silent, total,
# and blamed on the format rather than on the checkout.
#
# `-text` means: no conversion, in either direction, ever.
examples/05-a-real-signed-document.md   -text
*.pdf                                    binary

# Everything else is ordinary text and normalises to LF in the repository.
*.md      text eol=lf
*.mjs     text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
